tags: event

= Naturalization of Alaric Gallax

The leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, Alaric Gallax, remains a stateless person after renouncing his Freehold citizenship in 4290. Numerous attempts have been made by him and his supporters to secure a civil service appointment, as this would automatically grant him Commonwealth citizenship under existing law—making it the easiest path to naturalization. Citizenship is a prerequisite for Gallax to become President or Chancellor and would bolster his image as the "Führer of the Germans."

[? if thuringia_royalist: Wilhelm Frask, former <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> minister in Stathmore, has managed to appoint Gallax as Gendarmerie Commissioner in a small Stathmore town. However, for reasons unknown, Gallax tore up his own certificate of appointment. ?][? if brunswick_gallax: In the small Free State of Brunswick, a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> coalition has been governing with the support of the propertied parties. In an attempt to secure Gallax's citizenship, they sought to appoint him as a professor in secret. However, the scheme was exposed and halted due to his lack of academic qualifications. A parliamentary inquiry is now in progress, but further legal prosecution is blocked by the propertied parties. This revelation has tarnished his reputation across the Commonwealth. ?]

With the presidential elections approaching, it is likely that Gallax will make one final attempt to obtain citizenship.

- @brunswick: The [? if gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not gold_exist:[? if not concord_formed:<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if concord_formed:<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>?]?], in collaboration with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in Brunswick, appoints Gallax to the civil service.
- @brunswick_fail: The government of Brunswick attempts once more to appoint Gallax to the civil service.
- @nothing: With the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> being excluded from every state government, Gallax remains unable to be naturalized.

@brunswick
view-if: brunswick_gallax and gold_ideology == "Right" and gold_leader == "Coalfax" and not lvp_formed and not concord_formed
on-arrival: gallax_citizen = 1; commons_royalist += 3; burgher_royalist += 4; guild_royalist += 4; landed_royalist += 4; disfavored_royalist += 3; faithful_royalist += 2; pro_republic -= 3

In order for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> to quickly and discreetly grant Gallax citizenship, they had to collaborate with the [? if gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not gold_exist: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?], who, while supportive of these efforts, insisted on maintaining an appearance of legality. During a meeting between the two parties, they agreed to give Gallax a position in the Brunswick embassy to the Commonwealth Council.

Following this agreement, a heated debate erupted about whether Gallax would actually fulfill his obligations once he became a civil servant. However, after further reassurances, Gallax was sworn in and officially granted citizenship.

@brunswick_fail
view-if: brunswick_gallax and (((gold_ideology != "Right" or gold_leader != "Coalfax") or lvp_formed) or concord_formed)
on-arrival: gallax_citizen = 0; pro_republic += 3

In order for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> to quickly and discreetly grant Gallax citizenship, they had to collaborate with the [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist:<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not lvp_formed and not gold_exist:[? if not concord_formed:<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if concord_formed:<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>?]?][? if lvp_formed:<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], whose radical right-wing elements are in support, but the party as a whole opposes this move. During a meeting between the two parties, no agreement is reached.

As a result, Gallax will remain a stateless person, and this will damage his reputation as the Führer of the Germans.

@nothing
choose-if: not brunswick_gallax
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> is in control of Brunswick.
on-arrival: gallax_citizen = 0; pro_republic += 3; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2

With the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> being excluded from all *Länders* and *Freistaats*, they are unable to convince their governments to appoint Gallax to civil service.

As a result, Gallax will remain a stateless person, and this will damage his reputation as the Führer of the Germans.
